{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W4bRvqsUH6PKpkJzBF9eNC","type":"tool_result","content":"=== evidence rocm10 §11 ===\n11:## 0. Headline\n27:## 1. Fetch results and what landed\n29:### 1.1 Fetch output [M]\n51:### 1.2 Commit volume [M]\n60:### 1.3 `amd-strix-halo-toolboxes` — origin/main, last 7 days [M]\n72:### 1.4 `strix-halo-ds4-toolbox` — origin/main, last 7 days [M]\n86:### 1.5 `ds4-kyuz0` (`kyuz0/ds4`, branch `perf/rocm-gfx1151-mmq-kernel-lab`) — today [M]\n108:## 2. What the ROCm 10.0 update actually changed\n110:### 2.1 Exact ROCm version and repository move [S]\n134:### 2.2 Package-set change [S]\n160:### 2.3 Which images/tags\n193:### 2.4 The branch switch is the bigger change than the ROCm bump [S]\n209:### 2.5 TheRock nightly / rocBLAS — no direct change today\n221:## 3. Does kyuz0 publish a newer `vllm-therock-gfx1151` / a vllm+ROCm10 image?\n223:### 3.1 The toolbox repos are the wrong place to look — measured negative [M]\n238:### 3.2 The vLLM image has its own repo — found and read [M]\n256:### 3.3 Registry state — SETTLED, not undetermined\n297:### 3.4 Why no vLLM ROCm 10 image can exist yet — root cause [M]\n343:## 4. ROCm / TheRock version carried by each candidate base\n357:### 4.1 rocBLAS: the concrete ROCm 10 breakage [S]\n418:### 4.2 hipBLASLt and gfx1151 [S]\n427:### 4.3 gfx1151-specific work today [S]\n446:## 5. The Qwen3.8-Flash-Next toolbox was RETIRED today — directly campaign-relevant\n472:## 6. `nix-strix-halo` — ROCm 7.x, not 10\n501:## 7. The rebase question: 470229c → what?\n503:### 7.1 Placing 470229c precisely [M]\n541:### 7.2 The patch overlay is all-modify, zero-add — the rebase risk is total [M]\n567:### 7.3 Good news: the filesystem contract survives the distro change [S]\n603:## 8. What the QA doc says the ROCm 10 migration changed or broke\n636:## 9. Bottom line for the container-base decision\n662:## 10. Open / UNDETERMINED\n683:## Artifacts created this session (read-only probes, safe to delete)\n691:## 11. Correction (2026-08-30)\n---\n## 11. Correction (2026-08-30)\n\nThe §3.4 / §9.2 ruling — \"no ROCm 10 gfx1151 torch wheels are published\" —\nis corrected. The probe behind it checked\n`stable.repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/` (404) and\n`repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/` (capped at 7.14) but never\n`https://stable.repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-next/`, which has carried a complete\naligned gfx1151/cp312 ROCm 10.0.0 set since 2026-08-26 11:52 GMT (two days\nBEFORE this dossier was written): `torch 2.13.0+rocm10.0.0`,\n`torchvision 0.28.0+rocm10.0.0`, `triton 3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm10.0.0`,\n`rocm-sdk-{core,devel,libraries} 10.0.0`, plus the gfx1151 device wheels.\nVerified 2026-08-30 by enumerating the index and reading the torch wheel's\nMETADATA over HTTP range requests: same upstream versions and the SAME\ntriton git hash (`4cff872c`) as the 7.14 set — the fork's triton-version fp8\ngates evaluate identically — and an isomorphic dependency graph, so the\nmigration is a version-literal substitution, not a port.\n\nAlso corrected: §4.1's rocBLAS 5.5→5.6 solution-index breakage is\nds4-lineage-specific (hardcoded solution indices in llama.cpp-lineage HIP\ncode). The mecattaf/vllm fork at `bdb6f042` carries no tuned solution\nindices — the only `solution_index` reference is `-1` (\"library default\")\nat `vllm/_aiter_ops.py:714`. Open item §10's rocBLAS⇔ROCm-10 inference is\nmoot for this project.\n\nWhat remains genuinely unknown (and why ROCm 10 is still not the overnight\nsubstrate): no upstream anywhere has run vLLM on ROCm 10 on gfx1151 —\nkyuz0's own auto-discovery pipeline still resolves 7.14 with zero rocm10\nimage tags — so whether ROCm 10's hipcc compiles the fork's HIP sources and\nwhether its HSA runtime binds the in-tree KFD on kernel 7.2.x are both\nunmeasured. The `rocm10-probe` worklist lane (2026-08-30) answers both on a\nseparate image tag, off the critical path, writing its outcome OUTSIDE\nresults/receipts/ so a red probe is data, never a campaign failure.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14d5dc87-45ef-4522-8c3f-4943542b92cb","uuid":"1ac105e7-f1a5-434a-b247-600af0954346","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:08:01.033Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== evidence rocm10 §11 ===\n11:## 0. Headline\n27:## 1. Fetch results and what landed\n29:### 1.1 Fetch output [M]\n51:### 1.2 Commit volume [M]\n60:### 1.3 `amd-strix-halo-toolboxes` — origin/main, last 7 days [M]\n72:### 1.4 `strix-halo-ds4-toolbox` — origin/main, last 7 days [M]\n86:### 1.5 `ds4-kyuz0` (`kyuz0/ds4`, branch `perf/rocm-gfx1151-mmq-kernel-lab`) — today [M]\n108:## 2. What the ROCm 10.0 update actually changed\n110:### 2.1 Exact ROCm version and repository move [S]\n134:### 2.2 Package-set change [S]\n160:### 2.3 Which images/tags\n193:### 2.4 The branch switch is the bigger change than the ROCm bump [S]\n209:### 2.5 TheRock nightly / rocBLAS — no direct change today\n221:## 3. Does kyuz0 publish a newer `vllm-therock-gfx1151` / a vllm+ROCm10 image?\n223:### 3.1 The toolbox repos are the wrong place to look — measured negative [M]\n238:### 3.2 The vLLM image has its own repo — found and read [M]\n256:### 3.3 Registry state — SETTLED, not undetermined\n297:### 3.4 Why no vLLM ROCm 10 image can exist yet — root cause [M]\n343:## 4. ROCm / TheRock version carried by each candidate base\n357:### 4.1 rocBLAS: the concrete ROCm 10 breakage [S]\n418:### 4.2 hipBLASLt and gfx1151 [S]\n427:### 4.3 gfx1151-specific work today [S]\n446:## 5. The Qwen3.8-Flash-Next toolbox was RETIRED today — directly campaign-relevant\n472:## 6. `nix-strix-halo` — ROCm 7.x, not 10\n501:## 7. The rebase question: 470229c → what?\n503:### 7.1 Placing 470229c precisely [M]\n541:### 7.2 The patch overlay is all-modify, zero-add — the rebase risk is total [M]\n567:### 7.3 Good news: the filesystem contract survives the distro change [S]\n603:## 8. What the QA doc says the ROCm 10 migration changed or broke\n636:## 9. Bottom line for the container-