{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FckduTERwDSA2Cua1eNZaY","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"id\": \"cp-build\",\n \"kind\": \"checkpoint\",\n \"title\": \"Checkpoint: the container engine build\",\n \"argv\": [\n  \"bash\",\n  \"-euc\",\n  \"bash container/build.sh && python3 -c \\\"import json,subprocess,sys; head=json.loads(subprocess.run(['git','show','HEAD:results/receipts/build.json'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout); new=json.load(open('results/receipts/build.json')); inv=('torch','triton','fork_commit'); ok=(new.get('status')=='pass'==head.get('status') and all(new['data'].get(k)==head['data'].get(k) for k in inv)); subprocess.run(['git','checkout','--','results/receipts/build.json'],check=True) if ok else sys.exit('cp-build: receipt drift on contract fields: '+repr({k:(head['data'].get(k),new['data'].get(k)) for k in inv if head['data'].get(k)!=new['data'].get(k)}))\\\"\"\n ],\n \"runtimeMaxSec\": 14400,\n \"dependencies\": [\n  \"container-recipe\",\n  \"instruments\"\n ]\n}\n---\n{\n \"id\": \"rocm10-probe\",\n \"kind\": \"implementation\",\n \"title\": \"Measure ROCm 10.0.0 viability on a separate image tag, off the critical path, after the bench\",\n \"goal\": \"Measure whether the ROCm 10.0.0 substrate is viable for this fork on this hardware, without touching the 7.14 lane that served the night. Context: a complete aligned gfx1151/cp312 wheel set exists at https://stable.repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-next/ (verified 2026-08-30; wheels dated 2026-08-26; same upstream versions and the SAME triton git hash 4cff872c as the current pins, so the swap is a pure version-literal substitution) \\u2014 but no upstream anywhere has run this engine on ROCm 10 on gfx1151, and two failure modes are unmeasured: whether ROCm 10's hipcc compiles the fork's HIP sources, and whether its HSA runtime binds to the in-tree KFD on this kernel. This lane answers both as DATA. Build a second image flashnext:rocm10 from the UNMODIFIED container/Containerfile using its existing build ARGs (ROCM_WHL, TORCH_PIN, TORCHVISION_PIN, TRITON_PIN, ROCM_DEVEL_PIN, DEVICE_PINS at container/Containerfile:48-65 \\u2014 no recipe edit, so the banked container-recipe acceptance stays true): podman build --tag flashnext:rocm10 --file container/Containerfile --build-arg ROCM_WHL=https://stable.repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-next/ --build-arg 'TORCH_PIN=torch==2.13.0+rocm10.0.0' --build-arg 'TORCHVISION_PIN=torchvision==0.28.0+rocm10.0.0' --build-arg 'TRITON_PIN=triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm10.0.0' --build-arg 'ROCM_DEVEL_PIN=rocm-sdk-devel==10.0.0' --build-arg 'DEVICE_PINS=amd-torch-device-gfx1151==2.13.0+rocm10.0.0 amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151==0.28.0+rocm10.0.0 rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151==10.0.0' . (a prefetched wheel set may exist under ~/.cache/flashnext-wheels/rocm10/). Then, on the coordinator only, run a minimal GPU binding check in that image (--device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host): torch.cuda.is_available(), torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).gcnArchName, a small fp16 and a small fp8-block matmul, and importing the engine package. Record the ROCm/HSA and KFD versions the runtime reports plus the running kernel release (a green probe on a 7.2.0 coordinator is strong but not conclusive for the pair; a red probe attributable to KFD must be re-checked on 7.2.2 before ROCm 10 is written off \\u2014 say so in the notes field). Do not load the checkpoint, do not start a server, do not touch the worker. WRITE THE RECEIPT TO results/rocm10-probe.json \\u2014 NOT under results/receipts/: scripts/receipts-verify.py fails the campaign gate on any fail-status receipt in that directory, and this lane exists to record an outcome, green or red, never to fail the campaign. The receipt carries {step:'rocm10-probe', status, ts, data:{build_ok, compile_seconds, torch, triton, rocm_sdk_core, gcn_arch, cuda_available, matmul_fp16_ok, matmul_fp8_block_ok, engine_import_ok, kernel_release, notes}} with status 'pass' whenever an outcome was recorded. Never remove or retag flashnext:dev; never edit container/, results/receipts/, or the worklist. If the night is running late this lane is the first thing the operator drops. Boundaries: touch only results/rocm10-probe.json.\",\n \"deliveredBehaviors\": [\n  \"By morning the ROCm 10 question is answered with a measured receipt on this exact hardware instead of a guess\",\n  \"The proven 7.14 image and the whole receipt contract are untouchable by construction\"\n ],\n \"readFirst\": {\n  \"specSections\": [\n   \"specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md\",\n   \"IMPORTS.md\"\n  ],\n  \"styleReferences\": [\n   \"container/build.sh\"\n  ]\n },\n \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"rocm10-probe-recorded\",\n   \"description\": \"An outcome receipt exists outside the graded receipts dir, the 7.14 image survives untouched, and the receipts gate still passes.\",\n   \"argv\": [\n    \"bash\",\n    \"-euc\",\n    \"python3 -c \\\"import json; r=json.load(open('results/rocm10-probe.json')); assert r['step']=='rocm10-probe' and r['status'] and r['ts'] and isinstance(r['data'],dict) and 'build_ok' in r['data']\\\" && podman image exists localhost/flashnext:dev && python3 scripts/receipts-verify.py\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"dependencies\": [\n  \"cp-bench\"\n ],\n \"conflictDomains\": [\n  \"results/rocm10-probe.json\"\n ]\n}\n---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14d5dc87-45ef-4522-8c3f-4943542b92cb","uuid":"3985070e-f81b-4a0a-8913-ec187af81992","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:08:16.858Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n \"id\": \"cp-build\",\n \"kind\": \"checkpoint\",\n \"title\": \"Checkpoint: the container engine build\",\n \"argv\": [\n  \"bash\",\n  \"-euc\",\n  \"bash container/build.sh && python3 -c \\\"import json,subprocess,sys; head=json.loads(subprocess.run(['git','show','HEAD:results/receipts/build.json'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout); new=json.load(op