{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DhtqYHTJ6m6PjgGTRE1ub1","type":"tool_result","content":"26:#   DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n27:#\n28:# What changed vs the donor recipe (per IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2):\n29:#   - torch is pinned to the fork's exact pin 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 from the AMD\n30:#     stable multi-arch index (the index tops out there; no ROCm 10 wheels\n31:#     exist for gfx1151 — specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md).\n32:#   - torchaudio is OMITTED; we drop the audio extra rather than downgrade\n33:#     torch to 2.11 (torchaudio capped kyuz0's auto-resolved set there).\n34:#   - the engine is the flashnext fork (mecattaf/vllm, branch flashnext),\n35:#     built from source for gfx1151, not a stock vLLM ref.\n36:#   - designed for overnight iteration: bind-mount a fork checkout over\n37:#     /opt/vllm and a host dir over /root/.ccache (see container/build.sh);\n38:#     the editable install then recompiles only what a one-line patch touched.\n39:#\n40:# Wheel provenance: the torch/triton/vision/rocm-sdk substrate comes ONLY\n41:# from the vendor stable index (spec F.11). Generic Python build tooling\n42:# (setuptools, wheel, packaging, setuptools-scm) and vLLM's upstream runtime\n43:# dependencies resolve from PyPI as upstream vLLM does; none of those is part\n44:# of the pinned substrate.\n45:\n46:FROM docker.io/ubuntu:24.04\n47:\n48:ARG ROCM_WHL=https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/\n49:# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n50:# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\n51:# verified by pip's own resolver: torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on exactly\n52:# triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (anything else is ResolutionImpossible).\n53:# < 3.8 awareness (IMPORTS.md): the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on triton < 3.8,\n54:# so on this wheel the admission stands but the in-kernel upcast is bypassed —\n55:# fp8 dots ride triton 3.8's own lowering, and the fidelity checkpoint grades it.\n56:ARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\n57:ARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\n58:ARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"\n59:# The from-source engine build needs the HIP compiler + cmake packages, which\n60:# the runtime wheels do not pull in; devel files merge into _rocm_sdk_core.\n61:ARG ROCM_DEVEL_PIN=\"rocm-sdk-devel==7.14.0\"\n62:# The generic torch/torchvision wheels carry no device kernels; gfx1151 kernel\n63:# images ship as separate device packages (torch loads them from torch/.kpack/).\n64:# Without these the first kernel launch dies with hipErrorInvalidImage.\n65:ARG DEVICE_PINS=\"amd-torch-device-gfx1151==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151==7.14.0\"\n66:\n67:ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive\n68:RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n69:        python3.12 python3.12-venv python3.12-dev \\\n70:        git ca-certificates curl \\","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14d5dc87-45ef-4522-8c3f-4943542b92cb","uuid":"7e26af76-e010-4be1-b63f-cea1ab5194d7","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:08:26.330Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"26:#   DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n27:#\n28:# What changed vs the donor recipe (per IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2):\n29:#   - torch is pinned to the fork's exact pin 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 from the AMD\n30:#     stable multi-arch index (the index tops out there; no ROCm 10 wheels\n31:#     exist for gfx1151 — specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md).\n32:#   - torchaudio is OMITTED; we drop the audio extra rather than downgrade\n33:#     torch to 2.11 (torchaudio capped kyuz0's auto-resolved set there).\n34:#   - the engine is the flashnext fork (mecattaf/vllm, branch flashnext),\n35:#     built from source for gfx1151, not a stock vLLM ref.\n36:#   - designed for overnight iteration: bind-mount a fork checkout over\n37:#     /opt/vllm and a host dir over /root/.ccache (see container/build.sh);\n38:#     the editable install then recompiles only what a one-line patch touched.\n39:#\n40:# Wheel provenance: the torch/triton/vision/rocm-sdk substrate comes ONLY\n41:# from the vendor stable index (spec F.11). Generic Python build tooling\n42:# (setuptools, wheel, packaging, setuptools-scm) and vLLM's upstream runtime\n43:# dependencies resolve from PyPI as upstream vLLM does; none of those is part\n44:# of the pinned substrate.\n45:\n46:FROM docker.io/ubuntu:24.04\n47:\n48:ARG ROCM_WHL=https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/\n49:# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n50:# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\n51:# verified by pip's own resolver: torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 depends on exactly\n52:# triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0 (anything else is ResolutionImpossible).\n53:# < 3.8 awareness (IMPORTS.md): the fork's fp8-upcast gate keys on triton < 3.8,\n54:# so on this wheel the admission stands but the in-kernel upcast is bypassed —\n55:# fp8 dots ride triton 3.8's own lowering, and the fidelity checkpoint grades it.\n56:ARG TORCH_PIN=\"torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\"\n57:ARG TORCHVISION_PIN=\"torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0\"\n58:ARG TRITON_PIN=\"triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0\"\n59:# The from-source engine build needs the HIP compiler + cmake packages, which\n60:# the runtime wheels do not pull in; devel files merge into _rocm_sdk_core.\n61:ARG ROCM_DEVEL_PIN=\"rocm-sdk-devel==7.14.0\"\n62:# The generic torch/torchvision wheels carry no device kernels; gfx1151 kernel\n63:# images ship as separate device packages (torch loads them from torch/.kpack/).\n64:# Without these the first kernel launch dies with hipErrorInvalidImage.\n65:ARG DEVICE_PINS=\"amd-torch-device-gfx1151==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151==0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151==7.14.0\"\n66:\n67:ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive\n68:RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \\\n69:        python3.12 python3.12-venv python3.12-dev \\\n70:        git ca-certificates curl \\","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
