{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYCSBYzqP785gEsqk2gf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `git status --porcelain` prints nothing; the work is committed on `tally-work/flashnext-23639e390702/container-recipe`.\n\n## What I found\n\nThis was a reconcile attempt, and the lane's deliverable was already present and committed in base history (`17e75f5`): `container/Containerfile` and `container/build.sh` implement the full goal — Ubuntu 24.04, py3.12 venv at `/opt/venv`, the exact wheel set from `repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/` (torch `2.13.0+rocm7.14.0`, torchvision `0.28.0+rocm7.14.0`, resolved triton `3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm7.14.0`), torchaudio dropped, `--depth 1 --branch flashnext` clone of `mecattaf/vllm` built from source for gfx1151, `container/rootfs/` copied into site-packages, `/opt/flashnext/build-info.json`, ccache + bind-mount iteration hooks, tests-then-build-then-receipt ordering, and the MIT kyuz0 notice in the header. The `recipe-pins` acceptance passed on arrival.\n\n## The one real defect, and the fix\n\nThe header still asserted *\"no ROCm 10 wheels exist for gfx1151\"* and cited `specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md` — a dossier whose §11 (landed 2026-08-30 in base, alongside the `IMPORTS.md` §1 correction) now says the opposite: an aligned gfx1151/cp312 ROCm 10.0.0 set has been on `whl-next` since 2026-08-26. `DECISIONS-2026-08-30.md` §6.2 names this failure mode directly — \"a stale ruling in a cited document is worse than no document, because a future lane re-derives the wrong conclusion from it\" — so the correction was landed everywhere except the recipe header that a container-lane reader hits first.\n\nCorrected in `container/Containerfile:29-31`, comment-only and **line-count neutral on purpose**: `rocm10-probe`'s goal and DECISIONS §6.4 both cite `container/Containerfile:48-65` as the ARG override point that makes its lane a zero-recipe-edit build. I verified the ARG block still starts at 48 and ends at 65.\n\nPins, index URL, fork branch and image tag are untouched, so the banked `recipe-pins` acceptance and `cp-build`'s `(torch, triton, fork_commit)` receipt diff against the committed `results/receipts/build.json` are unaffected.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `recipe-pins` acceptance argv — pass\n- 50 packaging tests (`build.sh`'s first step) — pass\n- `scripts/receipts-verify.py` — 3 receipts, 0 violations\n\nOne thing worth flagging for the operator, outside my write boundary so I left it alone: `scripts/receipts-verify.py` has no `build` entry in `BOUNDS`, so claim 3.1's required fields (lane, torch, triton, wall-clock) are checked only for well-formedness, not presence. `build.sh` does write all four; nothing enforces that it keeps doing so. Adding a `_build` checker would need `scripts/`, which belongs to another lane."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":605,"cache_read_input_tokens":69145,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":605},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14d5dc87-45ef-4522-8c3f-4943542b92cb","uuid":"6104f09b-9f7a-47a5-9d73-8869daeb80c0","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:09:34.712Z","request_id":"req_011CeYCSAhtyCVsA8ufeUMVr"}
